MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: aa9506f8b8c580c448622cdfc193780a, type: 3}
  m_Name: Case3_Greenhouse
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CaseDefinition
  CaseId: greenhouse
  Number: 3
  Title: The Nightshade Conservatory
  Location: "Thornfield Glasshouse  \xB7  The Midnight Bloom"
  SceneName: Greenhouse
  MenuBlurb: A famous botanist lies dead in her locked glasshouse, beside a rare
    orchid that blooms only at midnight.
  Intro: 'Lady Agatha Thorne locked herself in her glasshouse last night to watch
    her Moonflower bloom: an orchid that opens only at midnight and has never before
    been seen in England.


    At dawn the gardener broke the lock and found her
    dead in her chair. The doctor says her heart simply stopped. But the door was
    locked from the inside, the key was in her pocket, and somebody walked through
    the mud.'
  Clues:
  - Id: GH_VENT_CRANK
    Riddle: Turn my wheel and the roof breathes in. Someone turned me after midnight
      with flower dust on their skin. Find me by the ladder.
    Tip: Look at the crank wheel on the wall by the ladder. That's how a locked glasshouse
      gets unlocked from the inside. Check the handle.
  - Id: GH_FOOTPRINTS
    Riddle: We walk without feet from the chair to the climb, small and muddy, left
      after midnight. Look down on the path.
    Tip: Look at the gravel between Agatha's chair and the ladder. Someone left footprints.
      Check their size.
  - Id: GH_POISON
    Riddle: Brown and corked with a warning in black, I hide on the low shelf where
      the spiders sleep. Under the bench on your right as you come in.
    Tip: Get down low and look under the potting bench on your right as you enter.
      Something poisonous is hidden on the bottom shelf.
  - Id: GH_GLOVES
    Riddle: Two empty hands lie by the purple light. They held the poison while she
      held her flower that night.
    Tip: Agatha's gloves are on the table by the Moonflower. Smell the leather.
  - Id: GH_TAG
    Riddle: I wear the flower's name on a little stick, but someone scratched me
      and wrote a new name quick.
    Tip: Look at the little name tag stuck in the Moonflower's pot. Whose name is
      on it now?
  - Id: GH_VISITORS
    Riddle: Every guest must sign my pages by the door. The last name in me never
      signed out.
    Tip: The visitor book on the lectern by the door shows who came last night. Look
      for who never signed out.
  - Id: GH_DIARY
    Riddle: I'm warm and I'm worn and I keep the gardener's hours. Find me by the
      fire that keeps the flowers.
    Tip: The gardener's diary is on the ledge beside the boiler. It tells you where
      Tom was, and what boots he wears.
  - Id: GH_SLIP
    Riddle: Dropped by the door, I'm proof that a young man was losing at cards in
      town at midnight.
    Tip: There's a folded betting slip on the floor near the door. Check the times
      stamped on it.
  CluesRequiredToAccuse: 5
  MaxAccusations: 3
  Questions:
  - Prompt: Who killed Lady Agatha?
    Options:
    - Ivy Vale, the rival botanist
    - Percy Thorne, the nephew
    - Tom Briar, the gardener
    - 'No one: her heart failed'
    CorrectIndex: 0
  - Prompt: How was she poisoned?
    Options:
    - Nicotine soaked into her gloves
    - Foxglove in her tea
    - A thorn from the orchid
    - Fumes from the boiler
    CorrectIndex: 0
  - Prompt: Why was she killed?
    Options:
    - To steal credit for the Moonflower
    - To inherit Thornfield
    - Over being pensioned off
    - To pay gambling debts
    CorrectIndex: 0
  - Prompt: How did the killer leave the locked glasshouse?
    Options:
    - Climbed out through the roof vent
    - With Tom's spare key
    - Through the boiler tunnel
    - Hid inside until morning
    CorrectIndex: 0
  SolutionText: '<b>Ivy Vale</b> could not bear Agatha''s name on the greatest discovery
    of the age. She signed in at 9:40, and while Agatha fussed over her orchid, Ivy
    soaked Agatha''s gardening gloves in <b>nicotine wash</b> from her own family''s
    nursery.


    She never left. She hid among the palms until midnight, when the
    Moonflower bloomed and Agatha pulled on her gloves to tend it. The poison went
    through her skin, and her heart stopped in her chair.


    Ivy rewrote the orchid''s
    tag in her own name. Then, with the door locked and the key in Agatha''s pocket,
    she climbed the ladder, wound the <b>roof vent</b> open and slipped out across
    the roof, leaving violet pollen on the crank and small muddy prints on the path.


    Percy
    was at the card tables. Tom''s boots would have left prints twice that size.'
  FailLine: The coroner writes 'heart failure'. Next spring the Royal Society honours
    Miss Ivy Vale for discovering the Moonflower.
  TopRankName: Master of the Midnight Bloom
  WrenCallOut: Psst. Behind the palms, detective.
  WrenIntro: Wren. Again. Don't make that face. A rare orchid is worth more than
    silver to the right buyer, and my client wanted this one. Now it's sitting in
    a crime scene.
  WrenWhoAmI: Wren. I find valuable things for people who can afford them. My client
    wanted to buy Lady Agatha's Moonflower, and a dead seller makes for a messy sale.
    Find me the killer and I'll owe you one.
  WrenSuspectsLine: Three people wanted something from Lady Agatha. Pick one.
  Suspects:
  - Name: Ivy Vale
    Role: the rival botanist
    Intel: Runs Vale & Daughters, the nursery across the river. She and Agatha went
      to war over who discovered the Moonflower. If Agatha's name came off that discovery,
      Ivy's would go on. She visited last evening and says she left at a quarter
      past ten.
  - Name: Percy Thorne
    Role: the nephew
    Intel: Agatha's nephew and heir, up to his neck in gambling debts. He inherits
      Thornfield. But he swears he spent the whole night at the card tables in town,
      and the club stamps every slip.
  - Name: Tom Briar
    Role: the head gardener
    Intel: Thirty years in Agatha's service, and she meant to pension him off next
      spring. He broke the lock this morning and found her. Says he was stoking the
      boiler half the night, then went to bed.
  DeductionTips:
  - 'You have it all. Start with alibis: one suspect was at the card tables, and
    one wears boots far too big for those prints. Who''s left?'
  - Nicotine goes through skin. She wore gloves to touch her orchid at midnight.
    Who had the poison, and the chance?
  - A locked door, the key in her pocket. The footprints end at the ladder, and the
    midnight pollen is on the vent crank.
  WrenSolved: Ivy Vale. Of course. My client will be delighted the Moonflower keeps
    its true name. Goodnight, detective. Don't touch the gloves.
  FinchCallOut: Oi! Detective! By the boiler, it's the only warm spot in here!
  FinchIntro: Finch again! I deliver the papers to Thornfield, and I sneak in here
    to get warm by the boiler. Riddles are free, as always. Wren's tips cost, mine
    just make you think.
  FinchWitness: I was dozin' by the boiler. Midnight-ish there was a glow from that
    flower, purple like a ghost. Then someone went creakin' up the ladder by the
    north wall, and a pane went squeak, squeak up in the roof. Didn't see who. Small,
    quick, smelled of flowers and tobacco.
  FinchSolved: The nursery lady?! That's front-page news! 'Murder Among the Orchids'!
    I'm off to the printer!
